SUMMARY:South Brisbane Cemetery moonlight tour
DESCRIPTION:Where it all began – a cemetery\, a torchlight\, and a thousa
 nd untold stories. Step back into the roots of Brisbane’s most beloved c
 emetery experiences on a Moonlight Tour \, the original night-time walk th
 at started it all. First held back circa 2009\, this was the tour that lit
  the path – quite literally – for every Friends of South Brisbane Ceme
 tery tour that’s followed. Unlike other tours with fixed scripts and set
  stops\, the Moonlight Tour is delightfully unpredictable. It flows with t
 he mood of the night and the curiosity of the group. No two nights are the
  same\, because no two walks through history should ever be! As you meande
 r beneath the stars and the towering trees of South Brisbane Cemetery\, yo
 ur guides – Tracey Olivieri and Liam Baker – will share the real stori
 es that have shaped this extraordinary place. They’ve spent years delvin
 g into the archives\, decades amongst the headstones\, and countless eveni
 ngs sharing their passion for the cemetery with others. You might hear abo
 ut: The floods that swallowed the past The evolution of headstone art and 
 forgotten funerary symbols The graves of the executed\, tucked quietly int
 o a shaded corner How faith divided the dead in life\, and in burial The c
 ontroversial “beautification” that reshaped an historical landscape A 
 whispered ghost story (or two)…for those who like their history with a l
 ittle chill And whatever questions you bring - because on this tour\, you 
 help steer the story! This is history as it should be: lived\, shared\, an
 d responsive to the wonder of the moment. Whether you’re returning to wh
 ere it all began or joining us for the very first time\, the Moonlight Tou
 r offers a rare and immersive way to explore South Brisbane Cemetery – n
 ot just as a resting place\, but as a living archive of lives once lived. 
 Bring your torch. Bring your curiosity. The story is still unfolding. All 
 of our tours are not-for-profit \, with all money raised going to our ceme
 tery history and maintenance projects.
LOCATION:South Brisbane Cemetery\, Dutton Park\, South Brisbane Cemetery\, 
 185 Annerley Road\, Dutton Park
